        ":question/problem": "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $P,$ given by\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 4 & -14 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -12 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $P$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 4 & -14 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -12 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 4 & -14 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(1){R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 4 & -14 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -10\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $P$ has $4$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $4.$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
